  "about": "Deprecation helpers whose arguments or closure cells state a rename or name a successor. Read by pymolt.delta.succession.helper_facts. kind: rename-parameter (old and new are parameter names; the helper makes the old name an alias of the new one), rename-object (new names the successor), prescription (alternative is an expression to use instead), prose (message is the deprecation text). args: roles of the positional arguments, in order (null skips one); kwargs: keyword name to role; cells: closure cell name to role, for wrappers made by the helper; call: true for a helper called in a body rather than used as a decorator. Each entry carries the fixture its test reads. wrapper: what the wrapper a decorator helper makes does to a call: warn (it warns, then calls the function with the very same arguments), keywords (it passes every keyword through unchanged, and may turn positional arguments into keywords), dispatch (numpy's __array_function__ dispatch: it calls the function), rename (it renames a keyword). A proof holds only through wrappers listed here with a wrapper kind: a forward through warn and dispatch, a keyword rename through keywords and rename too. types: the type of a wrapper that is no Python function. A rename-parameter helper that also maps values (values) proves no plain rename.",
